  "goodToKnow": "Einschulen means to enrol a child in the first year of school, mostly passive: eingeschult werden. Die Einschulung is a big family event in Germany: children get a Schultüte (a large cone full of sweets and school supplies), and there's a ceremony and often a party. Most children start at six. Regular: schulte ein, eingeschult."
